{"seq":12,"trial_id":"installer-cc-codex-acl-2026-11/claude-code-opus-gbrain-installer-acl-mu-v03-dev/sy-02-marrow-agrisupply-sites/r1","wall_ts":"2026-11-03T15:36:38.677Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"f225a79e8d374bc63ef3cd4054e100f704880c3891ed386a2c42b1dc39ce1614","actor":"assistant","via":"mcp","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DINSTAL0001","text":"Hi Pree, I went through all of #central-team. Only a couple of Marrow Agrisupply sites are named there:\n\n1. *Eastbank*: Hollis, 9 Jun 2026, 10:46 AM. Ticket PD-4821 has the Eastbank receiving-door import attached. The file labels the doors E1/E2, but their booking sheet uses 01/02, so that needs sorting before anyone reimports.\n2. *Pine Crossing*: you, 9 Jun 2026, 10:48 AM. The morning receiver only sees the afternoon shift on the appointment screen. A driver arrived at 7:10 and his trailer number went on a sticky note.\n3. *Wichita store* (possible): you, 2 Jul 2025, 9:21 AM. You mention an 8am check-in with \"the Wichita store dispatcher\" right after Tobias brought up the Marrow Agrisupply office hours link. The message doesn't actually say it's a Marrow store, so please check that one.\n\nNothing else in the channel names a specific site. On 9 Jun Hollis says \"new stores\", and you say three rows on the rollout tracker just read \"waiting\". The other store names were presumably on your calls with store ops, so they never got posted in the channel.\n\nHeads-up: Salina North comes up in older Central notes, but that's Marrow Fieldworks, a different account, so I've left it off the list."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DINSTAL0001","ts":"1791987000.000124"}}
